//! Release tooling for developers (`publish = false`, no `sim` feature): what turns a built
//! image into a release enclaves and guardians accept.
//!
//! - `trust`: the environment's `trust.json` from the log and the release and registrar keys.
//! - `aci`: the Azure container policy, generated by `az confcom acipolicygen` and rewritten to
//!   the release rules; its SHA-256 is `host_data`.
//! - `release`: manifests for a measurement (GCP: `seal_attest::gcp::measurement` of the image
//!   digest; Azure: `seal_attest::azure::measurement` of `host_data`), signed with M of N
//!   release keys, appended to the log and published to the control plane; an Azure enclave
//!   release also publishes its template (the `aci` output) for `seal deploy`.
//! - `identity`: a booted guardian's key, checked against its attested `GET /v1/identity`.
//!
//! The `seal-release` binary exposes each step, plus an SDK app (`app`, the simulator's flows
//! over a production SDK client) to exercise a live deployment.
#![forbid(unsafe_code)]

extern crate seal_client as seal;

pub mod aci;
pub mod identity;
pub mod release;
pub mod trust;
